TasksCheckboxesTooltip=Select optional integrations and actions. Shortcuts add links, file associations open supported maps in the editor, firewall rules allow multiplayer, and import copies the detected Heroes III data.
UninstallCheckboxesTooltip=Select only the user-data locations you want to delete permanently. Disabled shared entries are used by another VCMI installation.
InstallModeTooltip=All users: Installs VCMI for every Windows account, normally in Program Files. Requires administrator approval. Creates machine-wide uninstall information, registry entries, shortcuts, file associations, and the optional firewall rule. User data remains in the selected user-data folder.%n%nCurrent user: Installs VCMI only for the signed-in Windows account, normally in Local AppData, without administrator approval. Creates a per-user uninstaller and integrations. Other Windows accounts will not see this installation. Windows Firewall may ask for permission when multiplayer is first used.%n%nPortable: Keeps the application and user data together in the selected folder. Creates no uninstaller, registry entries, shortcuts, file associations, or firewall rules. The folder must stay writable; move or copy it to transfer the installation, or delete it to uninstall.
CopyH3FilesTooltip=Copies the detected Heroes III Data, Maps, and Mp3 folders into the selected VCMI user-data folder. The original files remain unchanged.
ReadyHeroes3Import=Heroes III data import:
